  {
    "number": 1284,
    "title": "Unify total computation across billable documents",
    "state": "closed",
    "draft": false,
    "merged": true,
    "created_at": "2026-07-07T07:21:00Z",
    "merged_at": "2026-07-09T16:08:00Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-09T16:08:00Z",
    "head": {
      "ref": "feat/1284"
    },
    "base": {
      "ref": "main"
    },
    "changed_files": 4,
    "additions": 72,
    "deletions": 39,
    "commits": 10,
    "review_comments": 4,
    "body": "## Context\n\nThe gross total existed in three copies: invoice, quote, credit note. A fix\napplied to one was not applied to the others — that is where bug #1279 came from.\n\n## What changes\n\nOne shared pure function, `computeTotal(lines, country)`. Rates stay in code, in\none table instead of three copies. The sign of a credit note is decided by the caller.\n\n## How I went about it\n\nFirst pass generated from the three existing functions. The result kept the\n`if / else if` per country, which I replaced with the table — otherwise we were\nadding an `else if` for every new country.\n\nThe generated tests only covered the nominal case. I added the unknown country,\nthe empty list and the rounding: that third case is what revealed the\ncomputation returned `0.30000000000000004`.\n\n## What I did not do\n\nMove the rates into the database. That needs a migration and an admin screen.\n\n## Review\n\nThree rounds with @sophie on the function name and where the module belongs.\nFixed before merge."
  },
